		BucketZombieBlog: Braineaters wearing a bucket taken from their former owner. These helmets successfully increased their defence and value.
		PrototypeSlimeBlog: The first batch of slimes turned away from Gods' grace. They were put into the recycle bin due to their destructive hunger.
		ScreenDoorZombieBlog: These zombies are heavily armoured, becoming a nearly unbeatable figure in the early stages, and thus sealed away in the shadow.
		ShyGhostBlog: A rather shrinking kind of spirit, being afraid of others' eyesights. Despite being locked away for millennials, they insist to offer friendly hugs from behind.
		MissleTurtleBlog: An aggressive variation with explosive blood flowing through their veins, ready to unleash their suppressed anger by blowing up anyone that's ahead of them.
		MagmaFlowerBlog: Exotic plants came to this world from a sewer. They somehow managed to spit burning sputum without setting themselves on fire.
		LivingNestBlog: Normally, Moss Hornets will lay eggs in those miserable victims, take advantage of their remaining temperature and turn their bodies into nests.
		EnchantedVineBlog: The grape vines that used to cling to the Gods' physique. They were never seen again after they are exhausted, unable to fruit anymore.
		ForbiddenJellyBlog: Natural products escaped from the divine garden of the God, they then were captured and confined for nearly five million centuries.
		RoseGardenBlog: Once they were the symbol of love, but their passion was decayed in the neverending torture. The only thing they seek now is blood.
		LostVikingsBlog: After being awakened upon the collapse of their jail, they will be searching for their long-gone homeland for the rest of eternity.
		AbsoluteZeroBlog: A collection of possessed spinning icicles. These condemned souls have been aching to feel the heat of the living.
		PrehistoricVirusBlog: Chaotic abomination of the Gods' ill wills. It was used to punish the atheists along with the floods and fires.
		DrillerBlog: Giant worms that have evolved in an incorrect manner. No one would expect their creation to fail this miserable way.
		FlyingCoffinBlog: Long sleeping spirits of ancient elites worshipped by crowds. In their indestructible boxes their wrath grows every second.
		WhiteCultistBlog: Adherents of the Gods on their neverending crusade to purge the heretics. They never realize that they've been abandoned by their lord.
		SolenopsisBlog: An invasive species taking the nests of antlions as their own. The massive damage they did to the local environment caused them to be banished.
		PharaohsHandBlog: Rumours say that the bandages used to wrap up a corpse will hear silent songs and start to dance in midair.
		ValkyrieBlog: Ancient harpy troop trained to fight for their lords' honour. Their loyalty drove them to become emotionless killing machines.
		WindElementalBlog: A high-energy polymerization of an element known as wind. Their entire physic being including their organs exist in the form of gas.
		SunlightDiscipleBlog: Both disciples and siblings of the Sunlight God, as known as the Sun itself. They are the eyes and ears of the God.
		ImpMageBlog: Imp summoners possessing great ancient knowledge. Rumours say that the fire on their tails represents their energy of life.
		MagmackerelBlog: Somehow the lava in the Underworld managed to actually live and form its appearance. They turn into fish-looking creatures to hunt.
		CursedLingererBlog: A part of this land's malice turned out to be having no goal at all, only to bump around and spread cursed flame everywhere.
		ChewingThingBlog: The wills of those gluttons that the corruption absorbed are so strong that they reincarnate as a pest eating away at this world, ever starving.
		EyeholeBlog: Deep down everyone has the desire to see everything, but few of them comes with a good intention. In the end, their yearning becomes a twisted nest of malice.
		SoulstareBlog: The desperate hatred toward someone transformed into an abomination able to kill through eyesight. Being too weak, they have to cling together.
		LinkPustuleBlog: At the final stage of this era where lights and nights have met a decisive battle, the immune system of this biome monster becomes more active than ever.
		ToothyBlog: All teeth under children's pillows are carried away by these flying monsters. They gather these resources to create new colleagues.
		MeatPotBlog: The Crimson is always intaking dirty waters, therefore from the pot there's no meatball or tomato soup, only kidney stones that need to be ejected.
		MicrorganBlog: These very tiny creatures have been tired of being predated and therefore decided to fight in groups. Their unity turns them into a destructive force.
		SlimySpiritBlog: Hallowed slimes are Gods' disciples blessed by, not one, but multiple supremes. They were expelled due to their defiant pride.
		GoldenEyeBlog: Supernatural phenomena with an intangible form. It's unclear if they're a delusion of hallowed power or the prototype of the warden.
		MonarchButterflyBlog: With their ability to instantly erase all will to resist from the minds of other individuals, these creatures are born to rule.
		DesertMimicBlog: To protect themselves from raiders, treasures in the tombs of ancient elites gained consciousness and hostility.
		TempleMimicBlog: A high-tech robot built by the disciples of the Jungle, responsible for watching over their home and collecting resources.
		PolarMimicBlog: Some buried their goods in extremely cold areas, thinking that none would find them and ignoring the magic of the land.
		AbyssSkullBlog: Revived from the forgotten past of the true buried city, they failed to escape from the horrible flood that destroyed their home.
		VoidWeaverBlog: Bizzare lifeforms that dig through space to enter this physical universe. They may have left a wormhole somewhere.
		ForgottenWarhammerBlog: Enchanted hammers possessed by ancient spirits devoured by the darkness. All they have left are timeless regrets now.
		DeepWeedBlog: Seaweeds grown above a place full of resentment can be aggressive. They can be used to make disinfectant.
		FluorescentAnglerBlog: This underwater predator is tired of eating fluoresent grass. It desires something fresh-and-blood.
		FluorescentSlimeBlog: These slimes fused themselves with fluoresent grass. Somehow they managed to learn how to swim.
		FluorescentMelonBlog: The very crystals of the magic of the glowing turf. It spits out melon seeds towards those approaching.
		DrownedBlog: Those who accepted the destined end stayed home and waited. The last thing they remembered is the sound of the turbulent flood.
		KeyStandBlog: Souls of the dead are said to be heavier than water, so they sank deep and attached themselves to the foundation of the city.
		WardenEyeBlog: The disciples of the prison's keeper. They follow the order of several powerful beings to eliminate intruders.
		ShadowSlimeBlog: The projection of a slime on the maze's wall. They seek physical forms and digest shadows of beings.
		ShadowZombieBlog: The projection of a zombie on the maze's wall. They prey on not brains, but spirits and intelligence of creatures.
		ShadowEyeBlog: The projection of an eyeball on the maze's wall. Their one-colored physique makes it impossible to tell which direction they're looking at.
		ShadowDiggerBlog: The projection of a worm on the maze's wall. Each segment counts as one projection. They connect to each other and swims on the maze's wall.
		ShadowOozeBlog: This sticky incarnation of oozy malice tries dragging any intruder, keeping them also trapped the labyrinth.
		ShadowArmorBlog: Ghosts of past warriors haunting the shadows of the walls. They endlessly roam the hallways, watching over the facility.
		ShadowChomperBlog: Embodiment of the material poured in from the other side. They are incompatible with the composition of this world.
		ShadowEaterBlog: From the leaking hole enters the macrophage of reality. Their only purpose is to devour shadows between every crevice.
		PurpleShadowBlog: Purple shapes that deny the rules of photon and spectrum. It's associated with the malice of lives.
		GoldenShadowBlog: Golden shapes that deny the rules of photon and spectrum. It's associated with the ultimate sacrifice.
		ScarletShadowBlog: Scarlet shapes that deny the rules of photon and spectrum. It's associated with a cosmic threat of hive mind.
		AbyssPortalBlog: Leading to another universe where indescribable creatures live, also been used by people from the ancient city in order to escape a flood.
		GoblinChariotBlog: Giant weaponry built by another league of goblins, who is fighting a civil war amongst the goblin tribe.
		BombieBlog: Great invention to let bomb drive a unicycle. They hunt down targets and and carry out suicide attacks.
		BigDipperBlog: An ancient satellite built for communication and positioning. It guides and gathers people from all walks of life.
		NodePointerBlog: The materialized body of memory address. Freed in the form of electrical current when not needed.
		PuppetOperaBlog: The puppet guides the world's malice away from people. The malice trying to escape weaves a stage and fate for the puppet.
		MoonlightsquidBlog: Giant monster that sleeps deep under the aquatic. Often mistaken with an evil mastermind.
		MoonlightsquidMinionBlog: These squids make beeps instead of bloops. They can fly out of water.
		RodBlog: Mysterious lifeform that feasts on high-altitude creatures' souls. It attacks with the solar energy stored in its body.
		RodMinionBlog: They're newly born rods following the Priestess. Always recorded by cameras but never seen by humans.
		MotherbrainBlog: The unfinished reincarnation of a tyrant's brains. This is the only hope left for the maniac cult around the dungeon.
		MotherbrainMinionBlog: The security system built in order to guard the last machine. Their outer covering is nearly indestructible.
		DiverBlog: One of the bottom predators with a structure can't be comprehended by humans from another world. Staring at this consumes your sanity.
		DiverMinionBlog: Parts of the Diver recklessly charging at preys. Despite their being away from their master, they actually share the same mind.
		WallofShadowBlog: A barrier between the Gods who created the balance of Terraria and the mortals who live in it. This wall serves as an obstacle sitting at the leakage point.
		WallofShadowMinionBlog: Being born from the ceaseless darkness, they are the embodiments of the worshippers abandoned by the supremes.
		FlyingSpikeSlimeBlog: Fragment dropped from the Sun God representing the red part of the Solar spectrum. They prefer dashing toward their enemy.
		PropellerSlimeBlog: Fragment dropped from the Sun God representing the yellow part of the Solar spectrum. They prefer crushing their enemy from above or shredding them with headgears.
		BeamSlimeBlog: Fragment dropped from the Sun God representing the orange part of the Solar spectrum. They prefer answering the call of the Sun God to doing anything else.
		OverwatcherMinionBlog: Three subsidiary clocks connected to the Overwatcher. They respectively represent the past, the present and the future.
		LifebringerMinionBlog: Direct children and champions of the Lifebringer, urged to expel every threat from the divine Garden of Eden.
		SonMinionBlog: The limb of the past soul who was lost but guided. They dish out ordeals, cooperating with the spirit they were following.
		OverseerBlog: Messengers inspected by the Overwatcher. Most abnormalities in time are produced via their very hands instead of the supreme himself.
		NitroSlimeBlog: Flying slime equipped with a jetpack driven by nitrogen. Its trace leaves a freezing mass of air.
		IcicleSlimeBlog: Armed with a head full of icicles, these slimes that comes from another planet knows to aim for the head.
		SnowflakeSlimeBlog: These slimes are covered in snowflakes that are formed under minus 274 degrees
		SlimeMercuryBlog: Sun's disciple, a celestial being known as Mercury.It travels faster than all other siblings.
		SlimeVenusBlog: Sun's disciple, a celestial being known as Venus. Brightness of its shine is only second to the surpreme.
		SlimeEarthBlog: Sun's disciple, a celestial being known as Earth. Rumors say that a civilization of mini humans thrives on it.
		SlimeMarsBlog: Sun's disciple, a celestial being known as Mars. Its presence often result in turbulent conflicts.
		SlimeJupiterBlog: Sun's disciple, a celestial being known as Jupiter. It's the only disciple with an unsettling red eye.
		SlimeSaturnBlog: Sun's disciple, a celestial being known as Saturn. Surrounded by a slimy ring that splits into phantoms.
		SlimeUranusBlog: Sun's disciple, a celestial being known as Uranus. This aggressively fanatic disciple leads the entire crew.
		SlimeNeptuneBlog: Sun's disciple, a celestial being known as Neptune. It consumes space carrying a great dark spot of void.
		SlimePlutoBlog: The hidden disciple associated with a celestial being known as Pluto. Only at a specific moment can its unstable trace be observed.
		SlimeGodBlog: In charge of Sunrises and Sunsets, he is even the Sun itself. Born on the first day of the universes' creation. Also serves as the cradle and destination of infinite slimy creatures.
		SpiritOfPastBlog: Time's disciple, the old regrets and unfinished dreams, rewinding the world to its original track by reversing the tape.
		SpiritOfPresentBlog: Time's disciple, the frozen present and the reality that should be grasped, halting the world's progress by stopping the record.
		SpiritOfYetToComeBlog: Time's disciple, the confusion, bewilderment and fear of the future, driving the world towards its destined direction by distorting the gravity of all things.
		OverwatcherBlog: In charge of time and space, deciding the seasons and borders of dates. Born on the fourth day of the universes' creation. He defined the lights and nights and made them clash.
		PillarOfMercyBlog: Life's disciple. It's one of the pillars supporting the tree of life. It represents victory, mercy and wisdom, unleashing the light of vernunft.
		PillarOfSeverityBlog: Life's disciple. It's one of the pillars supporting the tree of life. It represents splendor, severity and understanding, unleashing the light of acceptance.
		PillarOfMildnessBlog: Life's disciple. It's the central pillar supporting the tree of life. It represents kingdom, foundation, beauty and crown, unleashing the light of transcension.
		SuperProbeBlog: Concrete representation of the transcending concept "Kingdom". It guards the Pillar of Mildness.
		LifebringerBlog: In charge of life and consciousness, preventing the world from turning into a mess. Born on the third day of the universes' creation. She gives birth and support to all creatures.
		HydrologemBlog: First disciple of Matter, it operates in an eternally closed loop, taking the form of the water cycle. It is omniscient and omnipotent.
		PyrologemBlog: Second disciple of Matter, it hysterically renders all things incompatible, taking the form of electron contention. It is everything except omniscience and omnipotence.
		AerologemBlog: Third disciple of Matter, the eye of the whirlwind is the channel of thought. With material structures that capture consciousness and create sensory experiences, it brings everything before your very eyes.
		TerrologemBlog: Fourth disciple of Matter, represents the praxis of humanity in the real world, in the form of unit land and cultivated lands. The myriad souls concealed beneath lichen have created all miracles, constructing every deity with clay, text, images, or code.
		CosmologemBlog: Hidden disciple of Matter, it symbolizes the surmounting of an insurmountable node on the spiral stair. It's the peak of the wave and the apex of the spherical, singing a song of victory.
		UmbrologemBlog: Hidden disciple of Matter, it symbolizes the deceleration of the spiral and the consolidation of stubborn nodes. It's the valley of the wave and the bottom of the spherical, yielding in reluctant compromise.
		MaterealizerBlog: In charge of actual materials, forming and maintaining every single quantum. Born on the second day of the universes' creation. He separated the sky and lands from the boundless sea.
		ScarabBeliefBlog: In charge of mysteries, myths, and non-existence. It's more like a thought rather than an entity. It is also responsible for the conception of "god", meaning that this word is but a symbol for description.
		PythonBlog: Disciple of power and death, named White Snake, a creature that exists only in the past. She was once suppressed under a high tower, guarding her love in solitude until the end of time.
		ButterflyBlog: Disciple of power and death, named Emperor Moth, a creature that exists only in the past. Even though they die at the moment of reproduction, they spend their entire life moving mountains, offering the future to children.
		MammothBlog: Disciple of power and death, named Mammoth, a creature that exists only in the past. When the glaciers melted, he carried the polar paradise to the other side and fell at dawn.
		LoongBlog: Disciple of power and death, named Loong, a creature that exists only in the past. To protect the living, he extinguished a volcano with his own body and in that moment triumphed over death itself.
		TurtleBlog: Disciple of power and death, named Endless Land Turtle, a creature that exists only in the past. He rotates the fabric of reality with all his might, dedicating his entire life and all his energy to one thing.
		GriffonBlog: Disciple of power and death, named Griffon, a creature that exists only in the past. He promised to protect the people and glory of a kingdom with his life, never forgetting even when the kingdom collapsed, until eternity.
		EverlastingFallingWhaleBlog: In charge of power and death. A whale falls and millions thrive. Those who create new hope even after their own death and destruction conquer death and destruction itself.
		TheSonBlog: The "son of God" and the source of Hallow, who was sent onto the earth to guide the people. He sacrificed himself to awaken them but ended up unleashing the extreme spirit inside of him.
		TruthBlog: The true creator transcending existence and non-existence. All abstract and concret concepts hold no meaning for him. He in fact shouldn't be described as a "God". His only weapon is love.
		EnterFight_0_1: What's the price of climbing to the top? You asked, but gained light response.
		EnterFight_0_2: You shouldn't stare into my physique. Your visions will burn and the flame will never stop.
		EnterFight_0_3: Please, bring yourself no harm. Pause here and exit the game.
		EndFight_0_1: And so we danced to the end of the day. The dance was so beautiful it could reach and kiss the sun.
		EndFight_0_2: The grateful sun has nothing else but her own heart to offer.
		EndFight_0_3: Let its veins and blood carry you beyond the stars. May you fulfill your purpose following this long path.
		EnterFight_1_1: Do not think to break free from the chains. There's no possibility even for a single moment.
		EnterFight_1_2: The hands will cut you into ten billion pieces. You will scatter across time and have no place at where it ends.
		EnterFight_1_3: Accept its everlasting presence, but I know you wouldn't.
		EndFight_1_1: Do you think there is redemption for you? Along with everyone trapped in chains, yet exhausted their strength in the struggle?
		EndFight_1_2: Or, are you the starting point of the retroactivity that will save all the passed ones?
		EndFight_1_3: On this journey to break all chains, allow me to lend you an hour hand.
		EnterFight_2_1: You're finally here! I miss you so much. I miss your voice and your monologic eyes, and I've been waiting for a lifetime.
		EnterFight_2_2: How long will you stay? Don't tell me yet. Let's sing. Give me your hand and stay close to me.
		EnterFight_2_3: Let me cry on your shoulder, for just a short moment.
		EndFight_2_1: A lively song. A melody with notes higher than everest, and a refrain more lovely than the cherry on the cake's top.
		EndFight_2_2: You're going now? I understand. I never succeed in gripping you back. And I wouldn't expect for another chance.
		EndFight_2_3: Will you miss me? My love? Will you remember me？
		EnterFight_3_1: You can and cannot see the truth. You will revolve and adventure. And eventually, you will see the truth.
		EnterFight_3_2: But are you ready for the bloodshed? For all the sacrifices, burdens and sins. Do you see the risk? Can you withstand the madness?
		EnterFight_3_3: You can not prepare. No one ever can.
		EndFight_3_1: You have triumphed. And it won't last. The climax ends immediately. Your body will shatter, your bones will break.
		EndFight_3_2: But maybe, maybe your destruction will become the compass of something new, something carrying your pith.
		EndFight_3_3: I'm still revolving. You can not prepare. No one ever can.
		EnterFight_4_1: What's this? Severe anomaly indeed. My bag is full of dreams. Everything remains a myth. You can't profit from it.
		EnterFight_4_2: Maybe one is bigger than four, and quality prevails over quantity. But how does it taste? Think before you act.
		EnterFight_4_3: This is a one-way alley. Burn it with unseen fire.
		EndFight_4_1: I drift down the acid river! I saw pink cloud of death! I guess I will never stop. No skill was put to test!
		EndFight_4_2: Stop competing pathetic concepts like "void" or "emptiness" to "nothing" and "is not"! A worse blasphemy than echo block!
		EndFight_4_3: Nothing matters at all. Nothing matters anymore...
		EnterFight_5_1: Is that you? Have you come back from the next world?
		EnterFight_5_1_EasterEgg: Is that you, Mutant? Have you come back from the next world?
		EnterFight_5_2: I see. You're not. You're one of the others.
		EnterFight_5_3: Let's get to the point. You know why you've come this far.
		EndFight_5_1: I'm still falling even after that world's end.
		EndFight_5_2: Do you believe in miracle?
		EndFight_5_3: We'll see if the struggle ends here.
